.TH LIBTLS_TLS_INSTANCE_RETURN 3 "2023-04-01" "libtls" "TLS Library"
.SH NAME
tls_instance_return - Return from TLS instance operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libtls.h>
.sp
.B ssize_t
.B tls_instance_return(tls_instance_t* i, tls_op_t op, int ret);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B tls_instance_return
function returns from a TLS instance operation.
The
.B i
argument is a pointer to the TLS instance.
The
.B op
argument is the TLS operation.
The
.B ret
argument is the return value of the TLS operation.
The function returns the return value of the TLS operation.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B tls_instance_return
function to return from a TLS instance operation:
.nf
.B #include <libtls.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   tls_t* tls = ...; // Assume a valid TLS instance
.B   ssize_t ret = ...; // Assume a valid return value
.B   tls_instance_return(tls, TLS_OP_ACCEPT, ret);

.B   // Use the TLS instance

.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
